Z||000009||KissMySSFiero||12-20-2000||12:28 AM||||HEY GUYS THANKS FOR ALL THE COMMENTS.  IVE ONLY BEEN HERE FOR 3 MONTHS.  I DONT KNW ANYONE HERE YET TO PISS THEM OFF.  USUALLY IT TAKES ME SIX MONTHS ONCE I KNOW THEM.  ANYWAYS.  ITS DONE AND OVER.  IF I WERE TO HAVE CAUGHT THEM I WOULD BE IN JAIL NOW.  SO FOR MY SAKE I HOPE I DONT CATCH THEM.  EVEN IF I CATCH THEM THE COPS WONT LET ME GET AWAY WITH ANYTHING MORE THAN SCAREN THEM OFF.  SO I GUESS THAT IDEA WHERE SOMEONE SAID SOMETHING ABOUT FILET'S.....SORRY NO CAN DO....I HOPE EVERYONE HAS A GOOD XMAS.  IM NOT GONNA LET THIS ONE GET TO ME<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE  88FORMULA<BR>KissMySSFiero@netzero.net<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">  <BR>"There's a fine line between love and beer"||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroMaster88||12-20-2000||01:00 AM||||Wow, sorry dude...that really sucks!  I have way too much respect for cars to ever do something like that, no matter how pissed I am at the owner!  (even though I dont care much for SUV's or Minivans)  <P>And about the catching people in the act, been there!!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>This summer, I was staying at my good friends house.  We made our usual late night Taco Bell run.  When we got back, we noticed a car parked in front of his neighbors house with the parking lights on....we thought nothing of it, went inside and started eating.  About a minute later, the car left.  Then, every ten minutes, we heard a car go buy slowly, then drive off.  Keep in mind that my friend lives in a small neighborhood in the middle of nowhere, the street is in a U shape so basically 1 block.  His sister drives a 89 Chrystler Lebaron Drop Top.  She has a nice sterio system in it.  So, after about the 4th or 5th time hearing the car go buy, we go outside and hide in the bushes to see what type of car it is.  About 2 min later, the car goes by again.  It is a Cavalier Z24 drop top.  After seeing it go buy 2 more times (same car) we go inside and wake up his mother,  and she of course calls the cops.  After she hangs up the phone, the car drives by slow, pulls over in front of the neighbors house, turns off the lights and shuts off the car.  My friend goes to wake up his dad.  By this time it it about 3 am. When they get back, there are 3 people standing by his sisters car.  My friend and I sneak out the back door and up to the back gate.  We can see them perfectly, 3 girls!  All of a sudden, we hear my friends mom scream "You bastards" and we go running after the girls.  (remember they turned off their car)  We get to the car at the same time the girls do, and my friends mom, dad and sister about half a second later.  My friends dad and I got the drivers door opened and were attempting to pull the driver from the car but she had on the seat belt.  damn!  My friend was on the back of the car trying to get the spoiler (go figure), his sister had the pasanger (by the hair) and his mom had the wiper (like that would do any good!)  They got the car started (my friend jumped off the back), put the car in drive and started to take off.  All of a sudden, out of the corner of my eye, I see my friends dad raising his hand and it comes down and shatters the back window! (turns out he grabbed his 2"x2' stick form the closet which has a pipe fitting taped to the end of it!)  The girls sped off!  We went inside, called the cops again, and checked out his sisters car.  There was a 4" rip in the roof.  The girls were cought because of the description of the car, the license plate and the smashed back window.  They all pled guilty and had to pay for damages and write an appology.  If they come anywhere near us, they are in violation of their probation!!  Ooh, and by the way, the Police Officer told us that it was a good thing we broke the window, kinda marked the car and made their job easier!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>James||||reg||1
